The requirement states that after a driver reconnection following a previous failure, the ComStub must emit exactly one Fw::Success::SUCCESS via comStatusOut to indicate recovery. This requires:
1. First establishing a connection (which should emit SUCCESS)
2. Simulating a failure scenario (e.g., retry exhaustion leading to reinitialize flag set)
3. Simulating a driver reconnection (which should emit exactly one SUCCESS)
4. Verifying exactly one SUCCESS is emitted during reconnection

The test needs to:
- Use the existing test infrastructure
- Follow the pattern of previous tests
- Verify the exact behavior described in the requirement
- Use only the provided macros and methods

```cpp tester
void ComStubTester ::test_recovery_after_failure() {
    REQUIREMENT("SVC-COMSTUB-007");
    this->test_initial();

    // Simulate a failure scenario that sets m_reinitialize flag
    U8 storage[8];
    Fw::Buffer buffer(storage, sizeof(storage));
    ComCfg::FrameContext context;

    // Set up a send failure that will cause retry exhaustion
    this->m_sync_send_status = Drv::ByteStreamStatus::SEND_RETRY;
    this->m_retry_fail = true;  // Ensure retries fail and exhaust

    // Send data that will fail and set reinitialize flag
    invoke_to_dataIn(0, buffer, context);

    // Verify that failure was reported
    ASSERT_from_comStatusOut_SIZE(1);
    ASSERT_from_comStatusOut(0, Fw::Success::FAILURE);

    // Clear history to isolate the recovery test
    this->clearHistory();

    // Simulate driver reconnection (this should emit exactly one SUCCESS)
    invoke_to_drvConnected(0);

    // Verify exactly one SUCCESS was emitted for recovery
    ASSERT_from_comStatusOut_SIZE(1);
    ASSERT_from_comStatusOut(0, Fw::Success::SUCCESS);
}
```

