2. `PARAM_VALID` is not a member of `Fw::ParamValid` - I need to check the correct enum value

Looking at the F´ codebase patterns and the fact that `Fw::ParamValid` is an enum, I should use the proper serialization mode and check the correct enum value.

```cpp tester
void PrmDbTester::runPrmDbReadInterfaceTest() {
    REQUIREMENT("PRMDB-002");
    // Test that the PrmDb component provides an interface to read parameter values

    // Set up a parameter value
    const FwPrmIdType testId = 100;
    Fw::ParamBuffer testValue;
    U32 testValueData = 0x12345678;
    testValue.serialize(reinterpret_cast<U8*>(&testValueData), sizeof(testValueData), Fw::Serialization::MODE_BIG_ENDIAN);

    // Clear any previous history
    this->clearHistory();

    // Set the parameter value
    this->invoke_to_setPrm(0, testId, testValue);

    // Dispatch the setPrm message to process it
    this->m_impl.doDispatch();

    // Clear history before reading
    this->clearHistory();

    // Read the parameter value using getPrm port
    Fw::ParamValid result = this->invoke_to_getPrm(0, testId, testValue);

    // Verify that the parameter was read successfully
    // Since getPrm is a guarded port, it doesn't queue messages, so we check the return value directly
    ASSERT_EQ(result, Fw::ParamValid::PARAM_VALID);
}
```

